{"claim": "update_crates has no guard for a missing cmd/ crate: with cmd/Cargo.toml absent it dies at step 1 ('host build failed: failed to read cmd/Cargo.toml') AFTER step 0 has already rewritten the flowlang/ndata pins in place, stranding uncommitted pin edits in the working tree while the running binary was never rebuilt.", "detail": "Observed 2026-09-24 on the owner's checkout. The wrong recovery was also observed in the wild: hand-stripping the cmd dependency from Cargo.toml and the cmd-init block from generated_initializer.rs, which diverges from canon (canon keeps both). Correct repair: restore the touched manifests, regenerate the scaffold with newbound-agent tools/gen-cmd-crate.py (cmd/ is generated and gitignored), then re-run update_crates at the same versions — the equal-version repair re-run exists for exactly this.", "tags": "dev.dev,update_crates,cmd,git,repair,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1790259274005},
{"claim": "runtime/dev/update_crates/{run.log,run.sh,status.json} are TRACKED files in the newbound repo, so every update_crates or hard_reset run dirties the working tree by construction.", "detail": "Verified via git ls-files 2026-09-24 while diagnosing a confusingly dirty canon checkout. Until the paths are gitignored and untracked upstream, dirt there is runner residue, never authored work — and a blanket git add would ship one box's runner state to the remote.", "tags": "dev.dev,update_crates,hard_reset,git,gitignore,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1790259280560},
